### Derived physics you must implement and test (show the arithmetic in the tests)

```
g = 3.73 m/s²   (all values below use it; Earth g = 9.80665)

Free fall from 2.0 m:   t = sqrt(2h/g) = 1.036 s   (Earth 0.639 s)
                        impact speed = sqrt(2gh) = 3.86 m/s   (Earth 6.26 m/s)

Unsuited vertical jump (Earth reference apex 0.45 m): takeoff v0 = sqrt(2·9.80665·0.45) = 2.97 m/s
   Mars apex = v0²/(2g) = 1.18 m,   hang time = 2·v0/g = 1.59 s   (Earth 0.61 s)

Suited jump (energy argument: v ∝ 1/sqrt(total mass); assume body 80 kg + suit/pack 80 kg = 160 kg [SIM]):
   v_suit = 2.97 · sqrt(80/160) = 2.10 m/s
   Mars apex = 0.59 m,  hang time = 1.13 s   (same takeoff on Earth: 0.23 m, 0.43 s)

Walking (Froude similarity, leg length L = 0.9 m [SIM]):
   Earth preferred walk 1.4 m/s → Fr = 0.222 → Mars walk = sqrt(Fr·g·L) = 0.86 m/s
   Walk–run transition: unsuited Fr* 0.5 → 1.30 m/s ; suited Fr* 0.36 → 1.10 m/s
   Above the transition the gait becomes a bounding "lope" with a flight phase.

Wind force on a standing astronaut (dynamic pressure q = ½·ρ·v²):
   25 m/s storm gust: Mars q ≈ 5 Pa (ρ = 0.016) vs Earth ≈ 380 Pa  → ~76× weaker
   Force ≈ q · Cd · A ≈ 5 N on ≈1 m² vs weight 160 kg · 3.73 ≈ 597 N (<1%).
   → Storms must look and sound dramatic but must NOT visibly push the player or rover.

Sound travel delay: t = d / 240 m/s (a rover 100 m away is heard after 0.42 s).
```

**Gameplay vs realism:** default is the realistic values above. Add a clearly labelled setting **"Quick mode (×1.4 speed, simulation)"** for comfort; the physics (gravity, jump, fall) never changes. Keep the walkable area compact (≤ 300 m across) so realistic walking speed still plays well.

